          Modern rinse-off conditioners draw from a short but well-characterised roster of cationic actives, each with distinct chain length, counterion, solubility, and substantivity profiles. Small-molecule quaternary ammonium surfactants handle the primary cuticle deposition and texture functions, while cationic polymers (polyquaterniums) contribute lightweight film formation and antistatic performance — particularly valuable in fine or straight hair types where heavy deposition causes lank, weighted appearance. The table below summarises the primary ingredients used across the conditioning category.
